FILE: CLAUDE.md
FEATURE: example-redesign
DATE: 2026-08-26
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'changelog-requirement'

================================================================================
CHANGE 1 — Document the shared stylesheet
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
Every module gets a runnable example under `examples/<module>/` — `index.html`, `main.js`, `README.md` — served from the repository root with `data-id="vUX"` and `data-library-root="../../"`.

NEW_SECTION
Every module gets a runnable example under `examples/<module>/` — [...unchanged...]

The shared design system lives in `examples/shared/example.css`: tokens (palette, type, spacing) and primitives (`.wrap`, `.hero`, `.panel`, `.card`, `.status`, `.log`, `.err-out`, buttons, form controls). **Link it and build on it** — a page's own `<style>` block is for what is specific to that demo, not for restating the palette. Extend the shared file when a primitive is genuinely reusable; a page that needs a different look than the others needs a good reason.

REASON
The standard now has an implementation. Without this paragraph the next example would
reasonably start from a blank <style> block and re-derive a palette, which is how a set of
pages stops looking like a set.

================================================================================
CHANGE 2 — Retire the note about older, plainer pages
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
Existing pages vary: `examples/autowriter/` is the reference for this standard. The older `examples/modal/`, `examples/form/` and `examples/spa/` are deliberately plainer, because they demonstrate structural behaviour rather than a visual effect — bring them up to this standard when next touched, but do not treat their current state as the pattern to copy.

NEW_SECTION
All four existing pages meet this standard and are worth reading before writing a new one: `examples/autowriter/` for a live playground over every config property, `examples/modal/` for a component whose demo content lives outside the styled page wrapper, `examples/form/` for driving widget colours from the page's own palette through builder config, and `examples/spa/` for a page whose content is swapped at runtime and whose fragments must stay unstyled and portable.

REASON
The paragraph existed to stop the three unconverted pages being copied as the house
pattern. They are converted, so the warning is stale and would now mislead. Replaced with
what each page is worth reading FOR, since the four now demonstrate four genuinely
different styling problems — which is more useful to the next author than a ranking.
